packages/js/data/
# Both forms, for the same reason as the two Python lines below: the
# trailing-slash rule matches a real directory -- which is what
# publish-npm.yml's `cp -r` creates -- but NOT a symlink, because git does not
# treat a symlink as a directory. `make dev` creates a symlink here, and with
# only the first rule it would be committable. Committing it would defeat the
# whole mechanism: a fresh clone would silently work, and nobody would notice
# the link was missing until they checked out somewhere symlinks are not
# honoured and got a text file containing `../../data`.
packages/js/data
# Both forms, deliberately. The trailing-slash rule matches a real directory --
# which is what publish-pypi.yml's `cp -r` creates -- but NOT the symlink that
# `make dev` creates, because git does not treat a symlink as a directory. With
# only the first rule the dev symlink is committable, and committing it quietly
# defeats everything BUG 2 is about: a fresh checkout would silently work, the
# self-explaining FileNotFoundError would never fire, and `make dev` would look
# unnecessary until someone checked out on a platform without symlinks.
packages/python/src/algeria_wilayas_communes/data/
packages/python/src/algeria_wilayas_communes/data

# Build output
packages/js/dist/
coverage/
.turbo/

# Benchmark & tree-shaking artifacts
#
# results.json holds wall-clock timings, so committing it would make every
# `pnpm bench` run show up as a dirty tree. The durable record of the numbers is
# docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-008, which is reviewed.
#
# The visualizer emits `stats-<entry>.html`, so the patterns are globs. They were
# `stats.html` / `stats.json` -- filenames vite.config.ts never produces -- and
# 342 kB of generated HTML got committed past them.
benchmarks/results.json
benchmarks/treeshake-fixture/dist/
benchmarks/treeshake-fixture/stats-*.html
benchmarks/treeshake-fixture/stats-*.json
